<odoo>
    <data>
        <record model="ir.ui.view" id="view_working_schedules_import_wizard">
            <field name="name">ems.working_schedules_import.wizard</field>
            <field name="model">ems.working_schedules_import_wizard</field>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <form string="Session" js_class="ems_working_schedules_import_wizard_form">
                    <header>
                        <field name="state" widget="statusbar" readonly="1"/>
                    </header>
                    <sheet>
                        <field name="ready_to_import" invisible="1"/>
                        <field name="continue_disabled" invisible="1"/>

                        <!-- Welcome: file upload only - no validation/banners here on purpose. Resolving
                             an unknown e-mail/group, a missing classroom or a schedule conflict is the
                             job of the later steps, not something this screen should show or block on.
                             Every step below has its own short intro paragraph explaining what that step
                             checks and what to do with it (developer feedback 2026-08-10: the wizard has
                             many steps with no way to go back, so each one should be self-explanatory on
                             its own, not just the first one) - see docs/en/developers/employees/
                             working_schedule.md's "Import wizard" section for the full rationale,
                             including why part of this screen's own original text moved to the
                             "Existing schedule conflicts" screen's intro instead. -->
                        <div invisible="state != 'intro'">
                            <p>Import a working-schedule batch (one or several planner files exported from the timetable tool). Run this during next-course preparation, right after the previous course's schedules have been archived by the course transition wizard. Nothing is written to any schedule until you finish every step below and click Import on the last one.</p>
                            <group>
                                <field name="attachment_ids" widget="ems_blocking_many2many_binary" options="{'accepted_file_extensions': '.xml'}"/>
                            </group>
                        </div>

                        <div invisible="state != 'groups'">
                            <p>EMS checks every group name in the file against the groups already in EMS. Any name it couldn't match is listed below for you to resolve by hand.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="group_line_ids">
                                Every group mentioned in the file was recognized.
                            </div>
                            <field name="group_line_ids" invisible="not group_line_ids">
                                <list editable="bottom" create="False" delete="False">
                                    <field name="raw_name" string="Name found in file"/>
                                    <field name="group_id"/>
                                </list>
                            </field>
                        </div>

                        <div invisible="state != 'teachers'">
                            <p>EMS checks every teacher e-mail in the file against the teachers already in EMS. Any e-mail it couldn't match is listed below: pick the real teacher if it's a typo, or tick New if this is a genuinely new hire.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="teacher_line_ids">
                                Every teacher e-mail mentioned in the file was recognized.
                            </div>
                            <field name="teacher_line_ids" invisible="not teacher_line_ids">
                                <list editable="bottom" create="False" delete="False">
                                    <field name="raw_identifier" string="E-mail found in file"/>
                                    <field name="create_new"/>
                                    <field name="employee_id" readonly="create_new" context="{'no_create': True, 'no_create_edit': True}"/>
                                </list>
                            </field>
                        </div>

                        <div invisible="state != 'pending_info'">
                            <p>Nothing to resolve here - this is a preview of every teacher this import is about to create as a brand-new, pending-identification employee.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="pending_teachers_html">
                                No new teacher will be created - every teacher in this batch already exists.
                            </div>
                            <field name="pending_teachers_html" invisible="not pending_teachers_html" nolabel="1"/>
                        </div>

                        <div invisible="state != 'internal_conflicts'">
                            <p>EMS checks whether two different teachers in this same file end up scheduled in the same classroom at the same time. Each colliding pair is listed below for you to resolve.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="internal_conflict_line_ids">
                                No room conflicts were found within this batch.
                            </div>
                            <field name="internal_conflict_line_ids" invisible="not internal_conflict_line_ids">
                                <list editable="bottom" create="False" delete="False"
                                    decoration-warning="kind in ('co_teaching_eligible', 'desdoble_eligible')"
                                    decoration-danger="kind == 'plain_conflict'">
                                    <field name="left_label" string="File (left)" class="ems_conflict_label"/>
                                    <field name="right_label" string="File (right)" class="ems_conflict_label"/>
                                    <field name="kind" class="ems_conflict_kind"/>
                                    <field name="resolution" widget="ems_conflict_resolution" class="ems_conflict_resolution"/>
                                    <field name="left_space_id" string="Classroom (left)" invisible="resolution != 'reassign_rooms'" class="ems_conflict_space"/>
                                    <field name="right_space_id" string="Classroom (right)" invisible="resolution != 'reassign_rooms'" class="ems_conflict_space"/>
                                </list>
                            </field>
                        </div>

                        <div invisible="state != 'db_conflicts'">
                            <p>EMS also checks the new entries against schedules that are already active in the database - expected if this import runs against a course already in progress rather than right after a course transition. Each colliding pair is listed below for you to resolve.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="external_conflict_line_ids">
                                No conflicts were found against already-active schedules.
                            </div>
                            <field name="external_conflict_line_ids" invisible="not external_conflict_line_ids">
                                <list editable="bottom" create="False" delete="False"
                                    decoration-warning="kind in ('co_teaching_eligible', 'desdoble_eligible')"
                                    decoration-danger="kind == 'plain_conflict'">
                                    <field name="left_label" string="File" class="ems_conflict_label"/>
                                    <field name="right_label" string="Database" class="ems_conflict_label"/>
                                    <field name="kind" class="ems_conflict_kind"/>
                                    <field name="resolution" widget="ems_conflict_resolution" class="ems_conflict_resolution"/>
                                    <field name="left_space_id" string="Classroom (file)" invisible="resolution != 'reassign_rooms'" class="ems_conflict_space"/>
                                    <field name="right_space_id" string="Classroom (DB)" invisible="resolution != 'reassign_rooms'" class="ems_conflict_space"/>
                                </list>
                            </field>
                        </div>

                        <div invisible="state != 'summary'">
                            <p>This is the last screen before anything gets written, and none of the previous steps can be revisited afterwards. Review the counts and the existing teachers below, then click Import.</p>
                            <field name="overall_summary_html" nolabel="1"/>
                            <div class="alert alert-success" role="alert" invisible="existing_teachers_html">
                                No existing teacher's schedule will be recreated by this import.
                            </div>
                            <field name="existing_teachers_html" invisible="not existing_teachers_html" nolabel="1"/>
                        </div>
                    </sheet>
                    <footer>
                        <!-- "Continue" always occupies the same spot while state != 'summary' -
                             it renders enabled or disabled depending on 'continue_disabled', rather than
                             appearing/disappearing (developer feedback 2026-08-05). The second button is
                             a purely cosmetic, non-actionable twin (no 'name', type="button", static
                             disabled="disabled") shown only when the real one is hidden, so the label
                             never disappears from view - just its clickable state changes. -->
                        <button name="action_continue" string="Continue" type="object" class="btn-primary"
                            invisible="state == 'summary' or continue_disabled"/>
                        <button name="action_continue_disabled" string="Continue" type="button" class="btn-primary" disabled="disabled"
                            invisible="state == 'summary' or not continue_disabled"/>
                        <button name="import_planner_data" string="Import" type="object" class="btn-success"
                            icon="fa-calendar-plus-o" invisible="state != 'summary'"/>
                        <button name="cancel" string="Cancel" special="cancel" class="btn-danger"/>
                    </footer>
                </form>
            </field>
        </record>
    </data>
</odoo>
